# Shell

Tasks are the product. A board opens on the task list. Canvas is the second page, with a text label.

Redo in this order: tokens, shell, board list, task list, task dialog, canvas, then auth. Do not restyle one dialog ahead of the shell.

## Wide (>= 900px)

Left rail, 240–260px, white, hairline on the right. Top: current workspace name, tap to switch. Middle: boards in this workspace. Bottom: Settings. The open board is a filled row, not a new color system.

Main pane has the screen title and one primary button. Do not put a second app bar inside the pane.

## Phone (< 600px)

One column. Back returns to the parent (board → boards → workspaces). Title is the object name. No bottom bar with more than 4 items, and no icon-only tabs. Canvas is not a tab on the workspace home.

## What each screen is for

| Screen | Job | Primary button |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/workspaces` | Pick a workspace | New workspace |
| Workspace home | Pick a board | New board |
| `/board/:id` | Work the task list | New task |
| Canvas page | Draw on this board | none |
| Settings | Account and this workspace | none |

